From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <luke@agent54.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:18:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/50] controlledframe.setFrameRate(): the rate belongs to the guest, not to a frame sink

setFrameRate() set an interval on the frame sink of the guest's main frame
widget at the time of the call; after a navigation to another process the
guest had a new, unthrottled sink. content::SetRenderWidgetHostFrameInterval
is replaced by content::SetGuestFrameInterval(guest WebContents, interval):
the interval is kept as WebContentsUserData on the guest and re-applied to
the current main frame's frame sink (and cleared from the previous one) on
RenderFrameHostChanged for the primary main frame and on
PrimaryPageChanged. It is still one requester in the per-sink registry
(longest interval wins), so it composes with sources' maxFrameRate and
back-pressure as before.

Viz: FrameSinkManagerImpl::UpdateThrottlingRecursively(), which runs when a
sink registers, reset the subtree to the default interval and did not
re-apply explicit intervals, so a sink registered after its interval was set
(or a new child, e.g. an OOPIF of a throttled guest) ran unthrottled until
the next full update. Explicit intervals are now re-applied there too
(ApplyExplicitThrottleIntervals()).

Test: ControlledFrameTextureSourceTest.SetFrameRateFollowsNavigation
(setFrameRate(10): guest rAF < 14/s, also after a cross-site navigation to
another process; setFrameRate(0): > 25/s). With the other
ControlledFrameTextureSourceTest tests and CaptureStream: 30/30 with
--gtest_repeat=5.
---
