+// Experiment: the embedder's BeginFrame interval for a guest
+// (`guest` is the guest's inner WebContents; zero clears it). It belongs to
+// the guest, not to a frame sink: it applies to the frame sink of the guest's
+// current main frame and its descendants, and moves with the guest when a
+// navigation gives it a new main frame widget (e.g. another process). It is
+// combined with other per-sink requests (the longest interval wins) and is
+// independent of the other throttling above and of capture.
+CONTENT_EXPORT void SetGuestFrameInterval(WebContents* guest,
+                                          base::TimeDelta interval);
 
